#   stale_pending_rewalk:
#     label: STALE-PENDING-REWALK
#     ruling: 'PI 2026-08-30 (verbatim): "Temporal: NO all-106 sweep. #21''s wf-temporal regenerates its own T90/MVT/lag with the validated tools and REPLACES its rows in the catalog, keyed to the new receipt. The two campaign-wide wrong columns (lag sign, MVT) get a STALE-PENDING-REWALK label in the catalog header + a register row — every later burst repairs its own rows the same way, as it is walked."'
#     columns:
#       LAG: [LAG_S, LAG_ERR_S, LAG_SIG, LAG_ACCEPTED]
#       MVT: [MVT_S, MVT_ERR_S, MVT_TYPE]
#     lag_defect: 'LAG_S sign is INVERTED vs the standard convention (positive = soft lags hard, Norris+1996): the handbook DCCF was ported from a sign-flipped docstring (L26). Proof: SinglePulse_Temporal/notes/LAG_SIGN_VERIFICATION.md (2026-07-31, two skeptics, analytic + injection). Negating the column does NOT repair it — the value is the mu of a split-normal fitted over the full offset grid, not the CCF peak. Validated per-burst tool: scripts/47c (s02c compute_lag_dccf, unmodified import).'
#     mvt_defect: 'MVT_S is the Haar estimator, not the canonical Bala upstream; MVT_TYPE=detection is Haar-only. bn110920546: Haar 5.342 s exceeds the published upper limit dt_min<2.096 s (Golkhou+2015 Table 2, trigger 110920546) by 2.5x; the CWT cross-check (0.724 s) is consistent with it.'
#     rule: 'No consumer (report, paper assembler, accumulator, numbers-verifier) may quote a LAG_* or MVT_* value for a TRIGGER_NAME that is not listed in rewalked_triggers. A rewalked row is regenerated by that burst''s own wf-temporal with the validated, estimator-labelled tools and REPLACED keyed to its promotion receipt; the trigger is then appended to rewalked_triggers in the same write.'
